Package: freqseas
Title: Frequency-Domain Seasonality Testing and Adjustment
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Package", "Author", email = "grycrnwll@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Frequency-domain tools for detecting, specifying, and adjusting
    seasonality in time series, organized by the workflow's epistemic
    hierarchy. An extreme-value test detects excess mass at seasonal
    frequencies against a white-noise null (detect); shoulder and block-phase
    tests distinguish line from band spectra (specify); a declared phase rule
    fixes the filter-versus-components identification (identify); and
    seasonal-subseries-inspired gain surgery with the implied minimum-phase or
    zero-phase correction and whitener recoloring performs the adjustment
    (operate). Inputs may be 'ts', numeric with a stated frequency, or
    'tsibble' objects, and keyed series are mapped over independently.
